  "about": "When each page of docs/it-adoption/ was last read against the code it describes, and which files that code is. pnpm check:it-adoption fails when a watched file changes after the review, so whoever changed the code re-reads the page an organisation's IT signs off against. The watches are the few files where a change most likely changes what IT is told; that a named setting or MCP tool still exists is checked separately on every page. Re-stamp after reading with: pnpm check:it-adoption --record <page>. Reasoning: aimeat/scripts/check-it-adoption.ts.",
